    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a condensed active roster as we navigate a heavy schedule of team off-days. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Caleb Durbin** all sidelined due to non-game days, we are leaning on a lean, high-upside core. **Christian Yelich** earns our highest efficiency score of 59.12; while he faces a platoon disadvantage against the lefty Ray, the opponent's 4.98 xERA offers a substantial volume opportunity that outweighs the handedness split. **Junior Caminero** follows with a 55.12, maintaining a strong floor despite a difficult matchup against the seasoned Cole. While Cole remains a formidable arm, **Junior Caminero**\u2019s premium spot in the #3 hole provides enough plate appearance stability to justify the start.\n\nRounding out the lineup, **Chase Meidroth** checks in at a 46.70. His projection is bolstered by the leadoff spot and a moderate favorable platoon shift against Messick. While his overall profile is marginal, the scarcity of stolen base threats currently available\u2014made acute by the absence of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin**\u2014makes **Chase Meidroth** a necessary cog in our daily efficiency model. We continue to monitor the status of **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** to ensure we maintain depth for the remainder of the series, as the lack of secondary speed options from our bench players like **Carson Benge** or **Gary Sanchez** forces us to play the matchups aggressively. We currently carry no significant weather warnings, but the proximity of the scores for **Christian Yelich** and **Junior Caminero** suggests we should be prepared to pivot if late-breaking lineup changes occur for their respective clubs.",
